INSERT INTO `ha_term_relationships` (`object_id`,`term_taxonomy_id`,`term_order`) SELECT @translation_id,tt.term_taxonomy_id,0 FROM `ha_term_taxonomy` tt JOIN `ha_terms` t ON t.term_id=tt.term_id WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND tt.taxonomy='category' AND t.slug='iraq' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_term_relationships` r WHERE r.object_id=@translation_id AND r.term_taxonomy_id=tt.term_taxonomy_id) LIMIT 1;
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<p>Rainwater irrigation is one of the most advanced and efficient methods for managing water resources in modern agriculture, gaining particular importance in areas with irregular rainfall, severe temperature fluctuations, and dry or semi-dry climates. By simulating the natural rainfall process, this method enables the uniform and precise delivery of moisture to the roots and even the plant surface. In today\'s world, where water resource sustainability and cost optimization are critical issues for every farmer and greenhouse operator, a deep understanding of rainwater irrigation mechanisms can create significant differences in crop quality and economic efficiency. In this comprehensive guide, we will examine all technical, practical, and economic aspects of rainwater irrigation clearly and precisely, enabling you to make informed and sound decisions for your farms and greenhouses with a full awareness of the system\'s advantages and limitations. This system not only promotes plant growth but also directly impacts overall farm productivity by reducing environmental stress.</p>\n\n<h2>Fundamental Principles and Physical Mechanism of Rainwater Irrigation</h2>\n<p>This system is based on the principles of hydraulics and aerodynamics. In standard systems, water pressure is converted into small, uniform, and controllable droplets through specific sprinklers or drip emitters. These droplets behave very similarly to natural rain but with a temporal and spatial pattern adjusted by the user. This delicate process requires equipment such as powerful pumps with stable pressure, robust safety filters to prevent sedimentation, and tubes with optimal wall thickness to prevent clogging of sprinkler outlet holes. Selecting high-quality equipment suitable for the local climate is the first step in a successful sprinkler irrigation project. To better understand the technical and engineering standards of these tubes, study the <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/optimal-wall-thickness-tip-irrigation-tape/">Guide to Selecting the Optimal Wall Thickness of Irrigation Tubes</a> which can provide you with a specialized and precise perspective. Additionally, a deep understanding of how pressure works in lateral and main pipelines is the key to pressure stability and avoiding pressure drops at the ends of lines.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/راهنمای-جامع-آبیاری-بارانی-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="راهنمای جامع آبیاری بارانی - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>Sprinkler Irrigation Comprehensive Guide</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>Advantages, Limitations, and Comparison with Other Irrigation Methods</h2>\n<p>One of the most significant advantages of rain irrigation is the highly uniform distribution of water across the entire field or greenhouse. This uniformity significantly reduces root stress in sensitive plants and optimizes nutrient absorption. Additionally, cooling the air surrounding plants during the extreme heat of summer is a crucial secondary benefit of this system, greatly helping to prevent leaf scorch. However, all systems have limitations; with this method, high evaporation rates in dry, windy conditions and the potential increase in fungal diseases due to elevated leaf relative humidity must be carefully managed. Comparing this system to drip irrigation shows that while rain irrigation provides broader coverage, it has a higher energy consumption. Conversely, compared to surface irrigation, its efficiency and water savings are substantially higher. For a better understanding of the water requirements of different plants and the precise calibration of rainfall intensity, the <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/broccoli-harvest-per-hectare-guide/">Broccoli harvesting guide per hectare</a> can provide you with a comprehensive view of the cropping chain and water management. Furthermore, familiarity with climatic variables and their impact on soil temperature further underscores the importance of selecting the appropriate spray nozzle.</p>\n\n\n<h2>Practical tips for installation, commissioning, and maintenance of the system</h2>\n<p>Successful implementation of a rain irrigation system requires strict adherence to practical steps at every stage, from design to maintenance. The following are the key practical steps to ensure system efficiency and useful life:</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/راهنمای-جامع-آبیاری-بارانی-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="راهنمای جامع آبیاری بارانی - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>Rain irrigation comprehensive guide</figcaption></figure>\n\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Determining and adjusting system pressure:</strong> The operating pressure must align precisely with the working pressure of the spray nozzles. Excessive pressure causes irregular spraying and equipment wear, while lower pressure reduces efficiency and leads to insufficient coverage. The ideal pressure is typically between 1 and 4 bar, which varies depending on the type of spray nozzle.</li>\n<li><strong>Selecting the appropriate spray and drip equipment:</strong> The output droplet size must be suitable for the crop type. Small-leaved and sensitive plants require much finer droplets to prevent tissue damage. Sprayers with Tip technology are the best option for sensitive greenhouses.</li>\n<li><strong>Test for uniform coverage before planting:</strong> Before final setup and planting, use colored paper or rain gauges at various points in the system to check the precipitation pattern. Sprayer overlap should be a maximum of 10 to 20 percent to prevent dry or excessively wet zones.</li>\n<li><strong>Robust filtration network:</strong> Installation of mesh, sand, and magnetic filters is mandatory to prevent fine sediments, sand, and silt from entering the sprayers. Inlet water quality directly affects the health of the drip emitters.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p>Regular preventive maintenance of the system is of high importance and must not be neglected. Cleaning filters and checking for leaks in every irrigation cycle are critical steps. If your system includes tip lines, regularly inspecting outlet holes to ensure they are free from clogs and deposits is key to maintaining system uniformity. To learn about the process of selecting and purchasing drip irrigation equipment, which forms the main components of the rain system, refer to <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/drip-tape-guide-irrigation-selection-purchase/">Guide for Selecting and Purchasing Tip Lines</a> Please refer to this. Additionally, awareness of long-term maintenance costs can impact your farm\'s profitability; you can achieve this by reviewing <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/drip-tape-maintenance-costs/">the drip irrigation maintenance costs article</a> below.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/راهنمای-جامع-آبیاری-بارانی-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="راهنمای جامع آبیاری بارانی - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>Rain Irrigation comprehensive guide</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) about Rain Irrigation</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Is rain irrigation suitable for all plants?</strong><br>No. Plants sensitive to leaf moisture, such as certain strawberry varieties or plants with dense foliage, may develop fungal diseases if the timing is not properly adjusted. In such cases, combining rain irrigation with appropriate spacing of sprayers and greenhouse ventilation is essential.</li>\n<li><strong>How can system energy consumption be reduced?</strong><br>Using variable frequency drives (VFD) and optimizing system pressure during peak electricity consumption hours (network peak) are the most effective methods. Additionally, scheduling irrigation during the cool night hours significantly reduces evaporation and pump pressure requirements.</li>\n<li><strong>What is the appropriate spacing for sprinklers?</strong><br>This spacing depends on throw power and sprinkler efficiency, and the manufacturer\'s label usually provides a precise guide. As a general rule, a 1-meter spacing is recommended for 210 mm sprinklers, while 1.2 to 1.5 meters is suggested for 310 mm sprinklers. Performing a practical test with colored paper is always recommended to verify the final pattern.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>Conclusion and Final Recommendations for Maximum Efficiency</h2>\n<p>Sprinkler irrigation is a powerful and effective tool for improving yield, reducing environmental stress, and enhancing crop quality in modern agriculture, provided it involves proper design, selection of high-quality equipment, and correct maintenance. Combining deep technical knowledge with field observations and local climatic data can significantly reduce your costs and greatly improve final product quality. Always update system settings based on actual plant needs and the dynamic climatic conditions of your region. A deeper understanding of hydraulic principles and wise equipment selection represents an important and lasting step towards sustainable water resources and future-proofing agriculture. Attention to small details, such as the wall thickness of lines, can lead to significant long-term savings in repair and replacement costs.</p>','Comprehensive and Specialized Guide to AFP Irrigation: Principles, Execution, and Water Consumption Optimization','This comprehensive article examines spray irrigation in detail. Learn about its technical principles, advantages, limitations, and practical installation and maintenance tips to enhance water efficiency.','publish','closed','closed','comprehensive-guide-to-afp-irrigation-principles-execution-water-optimization',NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @slug_conflict IS NULL;
